          "quote": "(comp (ref \"R21\") (value \"0\")) ... (comp (ref \"R23\") (value \"0\")) ... (comp (ref \"R10\") (value \"0\")) ... (comp (ref \"R22\") (value \"0\")) ... (comp (ref \"R3\") (value \"0\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "two mutually-exclusive servo interface modes, selected at assembly time by populating different 0 Ω jumper resistors"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "PWM mode ... each servo header's signal pin gets its own independent 1 kΩ-buffered GPIO line"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The selected GPIO paths and MAX3485 serial output are connected to the shared servo-signal network at the same time. This defeats the intended mode selection, couples GPIO channels, and can cause signal contention or prevent reliable PWM or serial servo control.",
      "confidence": 0.98
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The netlist shows the PWM GPIO routes and the MAX3485 servo-signal route connected together through populated 0 Ω links. This contradicts the specified mutually exclusive PWM/serial configurations and risks contention and unreliable servo control."
